# ── Secrets & Environment ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Per-host env marker (written by install.sh, read by server.py
#    / bootstrap.py to re-exec into the correct conda interpreter).
#    Contains absolute paths — machine-specific, never commit. ──
.tofu_env.json

# ── Migration backups ──
.migrate_backup/
load_env.py

# ── Self-update backups (originals of files replaced by the tarball-overlay
#    updater for non-git deployments; reversible safety net, machine-local). ──
.update_backup/

# ── Data-cleanup leftovers (large stray artifacts at repo root, e.g. the
#    276MB delete.list.all.final; not part of the app, exceed GitHub's
#    100MB limit and break export/push — see export-large-stray-file note). ──
/delete.list*

# ── Python ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo


# ── Runtime data (auto-created, contains databases, configs, temp files) ──
# ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose: a bare `data/` matches a nested `data` dir at ANY
# depth, and it silently swallowed NEW untracked files under
# android/app/src/.../client/data/ (the android Room package — the 3 existing
# files survive only because they are tracked). Anchored to the repo root, the
# runtime dir stays ignored without hiding legitimate nested `data` packages.
/data/
# Runtime scratch under lib/ (tmp/, tool-results/) — rode the old unanchored
# rule; kept ignored explicitly.
/lib/data/
# ── Database ──
*.db

# ── Internal analysis (not part of the app) ──
/analysis_scripts/
/sundries/
/tools/

# ── Academic / personal scratch content (NOT part of the app — must never
#    be published to the public mirror). overleaf_cache holds fetched
#    Overleaf projects (real unpublished papers/theses); paper/ holds a
#    paper draft; thesis_references.bib is a personal bib file. ──
/overleaf_cache/
/paper/
/thesis_references.bib

# ── Personal scratch copy script (not part of the app) ──
/copy_to_chenxin.sh

# ── Export-stripped / not-part-of-the-public-product (DRIFT-GUARDED) ──
# These are excluded by export.py (ALWAYS_EXCLUDE_* / OPENSOURCE_EXTRA_EXCLUDE_*)
# but were committed BEFORE a matching ignore existed. .gitignore is the SECOND
# defense line (export is the publication gate / first line); the drift-guard
# tests/test_gitignore_covers_export_excludes.py asserts the two lists stay in
# sync so this gap cannot silently reopen. Documented keepers stay tracked:
#   scripts/gen_desktop_icons.py (CI icon gen), export.py, CLAUDE.md,
#   static/provider_templates/yourprovider.json (functional internal template),
#   scripts/package_extension.sh (builds the store upload zip; the SHIPPED
#     docs/chrome-web-store/ kit tells the reader to run it, so a clean clone
#     without it makes that instruction a dead end),
#   scripts/install_on_server.sh (server-side installer; same shape — a
#     documented entry point that must exist in a clean clone to be runnable).
/benchmarks/
/promo/
/scripts/*
!/scripts/rootless_egress_bridge.c
!/scripts/gen_desktop_icons.py
!/scripts/gen_tofu_icons.py
!/scripts/png_to_svg.py
!/scripts/build_frontend.mjs
!/scripts/frontend_budget.py
!/scripts/update_runtime_actions.mjs
!/scripts/verify_frontend_dist.py
!/scripts/gen_orchestration_authoring_metadata.py
!/scripts/gen_orchestration_compatibility_defaults.py
!/scripts/gen_orchestration_http_contract.py
!/scripts/gen_orchestration_wire_formats.py
!/scripts/gen_tool_inventory.py
!/scripts/audit_tests.py
!/scripts/bootstrap_rootless_qemu.sh
!/scripts/rootless_qemu-conda-linux-64.lock
!/scripts/rootless_terminal_bench_21.py
# P2 test tooling (docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md): test_select.py is loaded by
# tests/test_test_select.py and driven by `make test-affected`; ratchet_audit.py
# is loaded by tests/test_ratchet_incident_link.py and regenerates
# docs/RATCHET_AUDIT.md. A clean clone without them breaks both consumers.
!/scripts/test_select.py
!/scripts/ratchet_audit.py
!/scripts/package_extension.sh
!/scripts/vendor_mcp.sh
!/scripts/migrate_pg_to_sqlite.py
!/scripts/activate_sqlite_cutover.py
!/scripts/_database_leaf.py
!/scripts/migrate_chatui_to_tofu.py
!/scripts/compact_sqlite_diagnostics.py
!/scripts/compact_sqlite_projections.py
!/scripts/retranslate_truncated.py
!/scripts/storagectl.py
!/scripts/storage_certify.py
!/scripts/ptc_live_smoke.py
!/scripts/verify_pdf_stack.py
!/scripts/install_on_server.sh
# Shared "is this release complete?" predicate. BOTH gates in
# build-desktop.yml call it — the version gate judges an already-published
# release, the release job judges the artifacts it just downloaded — so a
# clean clone without it breaks the release pipeline in CI rather than
# locally, which is the worst place to discover a missing file.
!/scripts/release_assets.py
# Shared "is this VERSION documented?" predicate. The version gate in
# build-desktop.yml calls it BEFORE any build, so a clean clone without it
# fails the release pipeline in CI — the same worst-place-to-discover argument
# as release_assets.py above. It is also the reason nine versions (0.11.0
# through 0.15.2) shipped with no changelog entry: nothing in the repo
# referenced CHANGELOG.md, so no check could observe the drift.
!/scripts/changelog_gate.py
# Cache-waste distribution report. The measurement discipline it encodes —
# rates DERIVED from lib.cost rather than hand-written, non-waste classes
# (TTL expiry / cold start) excluded from the recoverable denominator,
# percentiles that treat 0 as a number — is the deliverable. An untracked copy
# means the next cost audit goes back to throwaway one-liners and re-makes the
# errors tests/test_cache_waste_report.py now pins.
!/scripts/cache_waste_report.py
# Second-path cache A/B probe. It is the control the gateway report is missing,
# and it is DRY-RUN by default — the value is the encoded experiment design
# (deterministic prefix, 4k to clear the cacheable minimum cheaply, and the
# size-dependence caveat that stops a cheap null result being read as
# exoneration). An untracked copy means whoever finally runs the control
# re-derives that design and probably drops the caveat.
!/scripts/cache_ab_probe.py
# debug/ = standalone scratch/benchmark scripts (never imported by the app);
# tracked *.log already ignored above, this covers the .py/.json/.png/.md/.html too.
# NOTE: contents-level (/debug/*), NOT dir-level (/debug/) — git never descends
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a /debug/ rule would make the negation below
# dead (the uploads/* + !.gitkeep pattern is the established shape).
/debug/*
# Whitelist: the CI wizard pixel probe (the manual installer-ui-probe.yml
# workflow drives it on windows-latest). That workflow ships in the
# opensource export, so the script must too — the same dead-pipeline
# argument as release_assets.py: a public clone without it carries a
# workflow that dies on a missing file.
!/debug/win_ci_shot.py
# Raw AI-gen asset candidates + proof strips (review-only, multi-MB) under the
# pet-icon dir. Anchored to that subtree, not a bare _candidates glob.
static/icons/pet/_candidates/
# Unreferenced marketing assets (~12.4MB) — stripped from the opensource export
# (export.py OPENSOURCE_EXTRA_EXCLUDE_FILES, zero-reference verdict 2026-08-01);
# gitignore is the second defense line so they can't be re-tracked silently.
static/images/tofu-cache-article-cover.png
static/images/tofu-cache-article-cover-zh.png
static/images/tofu-poster-core-strength.png
static/images/tofu-poster-v2.png
static/images/attach-icon.png
static/images/attach-icon.svg
static/images/onigiri-icon.png
static/images/onigiri-icon.svg
# setuptools egg metadata (regenerable build artifact)
/tofu.egg-info/
# Per-host helper scripts (hardcoded internal proxy IP / mount paths)
/setup_bashrc.sh
/copy_to_dst.sh
# Internal dev summaries / extension docs (kept in docs/, stripped from opensource)
docs/BROWSER_ENHANCEMENTS_SUMMARY.md
docs/README_BROWSER_ENHANCEMENTS.md
docs/README_EXTENSION.md
# Personal scratch answer PDFs (export ALWAYS_EXCLUDE_FILES; never source)
docs/解答260505.pdf
docs/解答260505_v2.pdf

# ── Eval / bench workdirs (large, causes FUSE timeouts) ──
# Glob covers every eval/bench harness output dir (swebench_workdir/,
# swebench_glm_ab_workdir/, swebench_pilot_workdir/, abtest_workdir/, …).
# These hold thousands of repo clones + conda envs (800K+ files combined)
# and are the #1 cause of grep/find FUSE timeouts — never track or scan them.
*_workdir/

# Hermetic evaluation outputs. The supported runner writes outside the project
# by default and also makes every artifact root self-ignoring; these root rules
# are the final guard when TOFU_EVAL_ROOT is deliberately placed in this repo.
/.eval-runs/
/eval-runs/
# Common upstream SWE-bench / Harbor output names, in case their CLIs are run
# directly from the repository root instead of through our wrapper.
/evaluation_results/
/sb-cli-reports/
/jobs/
/trials/

# ── CWD pollution: stray dirs created by eval/agent harnesses that wrote
#    output to a path RELATIVE to the repo root instead of an absolute one
#    (e.g. INS/your-username/..., mnt/dolphinfs/...; the harness stripped the
#    leading "/" and re-created our own abs path as a nested tree). Not part
#    of the app — see the 2026-06 "unrelated folders polluting the tree" note. ──
/INS/
/mnt/
/Mant/
/_/
/django/
/outputs/
/similar_fix.py/
/pylint-*/
# Root-level .project_sessions/ — a CWD-pollution variant of the per-project
# undo store (the real one is lib/.project_sessions/, registry-derived below).
# A harness wrote it relative to repo root; never track. Root-anchored so it
# does NOT shadow the registry-managed lib/.project_sessions/ entry.
/.project_sessions/

# ── Test coverage ──
.coverage

# ── Debug artifacts (developer-only, may contain API endpoints/keys) ──
debug/benchmark_results.json
debug/benchmark_speed_results.json
debug/prompt_output.txt
debug/ask.txt

# ── Logs ──
logs/
# Stray root-level run logs (e.g. server_15000.log written by restart_<port>.sh
# into CWD instead of logs/). Runtime-only, never source.
*.log
server_*.log

static/js/.bundle-*.js
static/js/.i18n-*.js

# ── Minified stylesheets (auto-generated at startup by lib/css_bundler) ──
static/styles-*.css
static/settings-*.css

# ── Frontend type-check harness (tsc --checkJs) ──
node_modules/
/node_modules.local_bak.*/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Linting ──
.ruff_cache/

# ── IDE ──
# Keep shared workspace settings (settings.json, extensions.json) committed so
# every collaborator gets the same file-watcher / search excludes — this is
# what prevents code-server / web-VSCode from spawning multi-GB fileWatcher
# processes on FUSE-mounted repos (see CLAUDE.md §9 cross-DC notes).
# Personal files (launch.json, tasks.json, *.code-workspace) stay ignored.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/README.md
.idea/

# ── OS ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Sessions & caches (auto-generated, may contain sensitive context) ──
# lib/.project_sessions/ is the per-project undo/redo store (modifications.json
# pre-image blobs). It is REGISTRY-DERIVED — see lib/runtime_layout.INSTALL_STATE
# / gitignore_lines(); do not hand-maintain a parallel entry. The drift-guard
# test_gitignore_covers_registry enforces this line matches the registry.
lib/.project_sessions/
**/.project_indexes/
.chatui/

# ── File-history store (per-project copy-backup undo data, auto-created
#    by lib/file_history; round-by-round GC churns it, so it must never be
#    version-tracked — see the 2026-06 "satus full of D" incident). This
#    file-history/ line is kept for documentation, but the trailing .tofu* glob
#    (bottom of file) is what actually ignores the ENTIRE .tofu/ tree — INCLUDING
#    .tofu/skills/, which is the per-project memory/skill DATA dir (export strips
#    all of .tofu, like data/). It is NOT source and must not be tracked. ──
.tofu/file-history/

# ── Safe-delete trash (files moved aside by the delete mechanism instead of
#    being unlinked; purge manually to reclaim disk). Never track. ──
.tofu_trash/

# ── Sensitive reports (moved to docs/ but should not be published) ──
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md
docs/RATE_LIMITING_DOS_AUDIT_REPORT.md

# ── Uploads (runtime data, not source — export strips the whole dir like data/) ──
# Ignore everything under uploads/ EXCEPT the .gitkeep placeholder that keeps the
# dir present in a fresh checkout. A broad uploads/* + negation closes the
# stray-at-root gap (e.g. uploads/cat_dog_manor.png) that the old per-subdir
# rules (uploads/images/* , uploads/pptx/ , uploads/papers/) let through.
uploads/*
!uploads/images/
uploads/images/*
!uploads/images/.gitkeep

# ── Model-generated posters (output of generate_image into project) ──
static/posters/

# Vite production output is content-addressed and rebuilt from frontend/src.
static/vite/
# Interrupted Vite builds leave temporary siblings beside the final output.
/static/.vite-build-*/
/static/tmp/

